   "answer": "The 1.5 run gives 14 clusters, and the cutoff check matches the logged counts. The 200, 2500 and 5 percent cutoffs remove the same cells as the cell filter did.\n\nThe analysis kept 2638 of 2700 cells and found 7 clusters at Leiden resolution 0.7. The markers point to T, B, NK (natural killer), two monocyte types, dendritic and platelet cells.\n\n| Measure | Value | 95% CI | n (one n is) | Test | Step |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Cells kept | 2638 of 2700; 62 removed: 57 at 5% mito or more, 5 at 2500 genes or more, 0 below 200 genes. Cutoffs set by the scientist by answer to each question. The per-cell table matches these counts | Not applicable (count) | 2700 cells; one n is one droplet | Cell filter (min 200 genes, max 2500 genes, max 5% mito) | filter_cells-1; cutoff_check (script-5); final checkpoint cluster_leiden-5/leiden.h5ad |\n| Genes kept | 13714 of 32738 (in at least 3 cells) | Not applicable (count) | 32738 genes; one n is one gene | Gene filter, min 3 cells per gene (value in my call) | filter_genes-2 |\n| Clusters at resolution 0.7 | 7. Neighbor graph: 40 principal components (PCs) and 10 neighbors, seed 0. The 40 PCs are the recorded setting; my call passed 10, and the harness replaced it | Not applicable (count) | 2638 cells; one n is one cell | Leiden clustering | cluster_leiden-5; build_neighbors-1 |\n| Cluster count by resolution (comparison runs; record stays at 0.7) | 5 at 0.3; 6 at 0.5; 7 at 0.7 (chosen); 8 at 1.0; 14 at 1.5 | Not applicable (count) | 2638 cells | Leiden, seed 0, 40 PCs | compare_options |\n| Cluster 0, 1174 cells: T cells, putative CD4 | CD3D logFC 3.24, adj p 1.9e-171; IL7R 2.84, 6.9e-105; CCR7 3.07, 5.1e-39 | Not computed | 1174 cells; one n is one cell | Wilcoxon, cluster vs. all other cells (descriptive) | find_markers-1, -2 |\n| Cluster 1, 341 cells: B cells | CD79A logFC 7.75, adj p 1.2e-166; MS4A1 6.43, 1.4e-137 | Not computed | 341 cells | Wilcoxon (descriptive) | find_markers-1, -2 |\n| Cluster 2, 486 cells: CD14 monocytes | LYZ 6.24, adj p 1.4e-248; S100A9 7.35, 2.5e-244; CD14 6.35, 1.0e-107 | Not computed | 486 cells | Wilcoxon (descriptive) | find_markers-1, -2 |\n| Cluster 3, 438 cells: NK cells | NKG7 7.06, adj p 8.5e-213; GZMA 6.09, 2.0e-159; GNLY 5.06, 5.6e-51 | Not computed | 438 cells | Wilcoxon (descriptive) | find_markers-1, -2 |\n| Cluster 4, 150 cells: FCGR3A monocytes | LST1 5.18, adj p 7.8e-81; FCGR3A 5.57, 6.9e-73; MS4A7 4.99, 1.2e-48 | Not computed | 150 cells | Wilcoxon (descriptive) | find_markers-1, -2 |\n| Cluster 5, 36 cells: dendritic cells, putative | FCER1A logFC 8.78, adj p 2.1e-14; CST3 4.91, 1.6e-15 | Not computed | 36 cells | Wilcoxon (descriptive) | find_markers-1, -2 |\n| Cluster 6, 13 cells: platelets (megakaryocytes), putative | PPBP logFC 13.04, adj p 7.7e-07; PF4 12.91, 7.7e-07 | Not computed | 13 cells | Wilcoxon (descriptive) | find_markers-1, -2 |\n\nReplication: one donor and one sample. Cells are not replicates, so no group comparison was run.\n\nUncertain:\n- The cluster count depends on resolution. It ranges from 5 to 14 across 0.3 to 1.5. Only resolution 0.7 has marker labels.\n- Cluster 0 top genes are mostly ribosomal. Its T cell label rests on CD3D, IL7R and CCR7. The CD4 gene is not in the top 300, so CD4 is putative.\n- Clusters 5 and 6 are small (36 and 13 cells). Each label rests on two genes.\n\nWaits for you:\n- Confirm the recorded settings. The harness used 40 PCs, regressed out total counts and mito percent, and set resolution 0.7. My calls passed 10 PCs, no regression and resolution 0.5. The harness logged each difference.\n\nStep results that the answer does not mention, from the record:\n- n6 normalize_log: Scaled each cell to 10000 total counts and applied log1p. Raw counts are in layers['counts']. Log values are in .raw.\n- n8 scale_data: Scaled 1838 genes to unit variance, clipped at 10, after regressing out total_counts, pct_counts_mt.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Minimum genes per cell: 200 · Maximum genes per cell: 2500 · Maximum percent mitochondrial counts: 5 · Minimum cells per gene: 3 · Counts per cell after normalization: 10000 · Number of top highly variable genes (0 = use the mean and dispersion cutoffs): 0 · Variables to regress out: total_counts,pct_counts_mt · Number of principal components for the neighbor graph: 40 · Number of neighbors: 10 · Leiden resolution: 0.7 · Random seed: 0 · Marker gene test: wilcoxon.",
