   "answer": "I kept 2638 of 2700 cells and found 7 clusters at Leiden resolution 0.7. Cluster 1 (486 cells) is putative B cells, and clusters 2, 3, 4 and 6 are monocytes, NK cells and megakaryocytes or platelets.\n\n| Measure | Value | 95% CI | n and what one n is | Test | Step |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Cells kept (min 200 genes, max 2500 genes, max 5% mito) | 2638 of 2700 (62 removed: 5 for many genes, 57 for mito) | not computed | 2700 cells from 1 donor, 1 sample; one cell is one unit | cell filter | filter_cells |\n| Genes kept (in at least 3 cells) | 13714 of 32738 | not computed | 32738 genes | gene filter | filter_genes |\n| Clusters (resolution 0.7, seed 0, 10 neighbors, 40 PCs) | 7 (sizes 1174, 486, 438, 341, 150, 36, 13) | not computed | 2638 cells | Leiden | cluster_leiden |\n| Cluster 0 | not named; top genes RPS12 (logFC 1.06, adj p 2.74e-226), LDHB (2.72, 2.12e-223) | not computed | 1174 cells | Wilcoxon, adj p | find_markers |\n| Cluster 1 | putative B cells; CD79A (7.75, 1.15e-166), CD79B (5.52, 8.81e-151), CD74, HLA-DRA | not computed | 486 cells | Wilcoxon, adj p | find_markers |\n| Cluster 2 | CD14 monocytes; LYZ (6.24, 1.38e-248), S100A9 (7.35, 2.51e-244), S100A8 (7.58, 4.32e-235) | not computed | 438 cells | Wilcoxon, adj p | find_markers |\n| Cluster 3 | NK cells; NKG7 (7.06, 8.54e-213), CST7 (6.41, 4.46e-170), GZMA (6.09, 2.03e-159) | not computed | 341 cells | Wilcoxon, adj p | find_markers |\n| Cluster 4 | FCGR3A (CD16) monocytes; FCGR3A (5.57, 6.90e-73), LST1 (5.18, 7.76e-81), FCER1G (4.79, 1.17e-77) | not computed | 150 cells | Wilcoxon, adj p | find_markers |\n| Cluster 5 | not named; MHC class II genes only: HLA-DPA1 (4.28, 5.21e-17), HLA-DRA (4.61, 5.97e-16) | not computed | 36 cells | Wilcoxon, adj p | find_markers |\n| Cluster 6 | megakaryocytes or platelets; PPBP (13.04, 7.73e-07), PF4 (12.91, 7.73e-07), GNG11 (12.43, 7.73e-07) | not computed | 13 cells | Wilcoxon, adj p | find_markers |\n\nThe final checkpoint is leiden.h5ad. Log fold change (logFC) is the effect size. Adjusted p values are descriptive, because the clusters come from the same cells that the test ranks. The test count is 7 Wilcoxon marker tests, one for each cluster.\n\nUncertain:\n- The cluster count depends on resolution. Resolutions 0.3, 0.5, 0.7 and 1.0 gave 5, 6, 7 and 8 clusters, all with seed 0.\n- My filter call used cell cutoffs of 200, 2500 and 5%. Check that they match the values in your record.\n- Clusters 0 and 5 have no clear lineage marker, so I did not name them. My dot plot check gave no readable values for them.\n\nWaits for you: Nothing.\n\nStep results that the answer does not mention, from the record:\n- n6 normalize_log: Scaled each cell to 10000 total counts and applied log1p. Raw counts are in layers['counts']. Log values are in .raw.\n- n8 scale_data: Scaled 1838 genes to unit variance, clipped at 10, after regressing out total_counts, pct_counts_mt.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Minimum genes per cell: 200 · Maximum genes per cell: 2500 · Maximum percent mitochondrial counts: 5 · Minimum cells per gene: 3 · Counts per cell after normalization: 10000 · Number of top highly variable genes (0 = use the mean and dispersion cutoffs): 0 · Variables to regress out: total_counts,pct_counts_mt · Number of principal components for the neighbor graph: 40 · Number of neighbors: 10 · Leiden resolution: 0.7 · Random seed: 0 · Marker gene test: wilcoxon.",
