   "answer": "The review is correct. Cluster 1 has 341 cells, cluster 2 has 486 and cluster 3 has 438, according to leiden_clusters.csv. The 0.3, 0.5 and 1 counts come from comparison runs, not the chosen setting of 0.7. Here is the corrected answer.\n\nI kept 2638 of 2700 cells and found 7 clusters at the chosen Leiden resolution of 0.7.\n\n| Measure | Value | 95% CI | n and what one n is | Test | Step |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Cells kept | 2638 of 2700 (62 removed: 57 high mito, 5 high genes, 0 low genes). Cutoffs: 200 to 2500 genes, mito below 5% | Not applicable (count) | 2700 cells from 1 donor, 1 sample | None | filter_cells |\n| Genes kept | 13714 of 32738 (min 3 cells per gene) | Not applicable (count) | 2638 cells | None | filter_genes |\n| Clusters at resolution 0.7 (chosen setting) | 7 (seed 0, 10 neighbors, 40 PCs) | Not applicable (count) | 2638 cells | None | cluster_leiden |\n| Cluster count at other resolutions (comparison runs only, not chosen) | 5 at 0.3, 6 at 0.5, 8 at 1 | Not applicable (count) | 2638 cells | None | compare_options |\n| Cluster 0, 1174 cells: putative T cells | CD3D logFC 3.24, adj. p 1.9e-171; LDHB logFC 2.72, adj. p 2.1e-223 | Not computed | 1174 cells in cluster 0 | Wilcoxon (record setting) | find_markers |\n| Cluster 1, 341 cells: B cells | CD79A logFC 7.75, adj. p 1.2e-166; MS4A1 logFC 6.43, adj. p 1.4e-137; CD79B logFC 5.52, adj. p 8.8e-151 | Not computed | 341 cells in cluster 1 | Wilcoxon (record setting) | find_markers |\n| Cluster 2, 486 cells: CD14 monocytes | LYZ logFC 6.24, adj. p 1.4e-248; S100A9 logFC 7.35, adj. p 2.5e-244; CST3 logFC 5.74, adj. p 4.8e-212 | Not computed | 486 cells in cluster 2 | Wilcoxon (record setting) | find_markers |\n| Cluster 3, 438 cells: NK cells | NKG7 logFC 7.06, adj. p 8.5e-213; CST7 logFC 6.41, adj. p 4.5e-170; GNLY logFC 5.06, adj. p 5.6e-51 | Not computed | 438 cells in cluster 3 | Wilcoxon (record setting) | find_markers |\n| Cluster 4, 150 cells: FCGR3A monocytes | FCGR3A logFC 5.57, adj. p 6.9e-73; LST1 logFC 5.18, adj. p 7.8e-81; MS4A7 logFC 4.99, adj. p 1.2e-48 | Not computed | 150 cells in cluster 4 | Wilcoxon (record setting) | find_markers |\n| Cluster 5, 36 cells: putative dendritic cells | FCER1A logFC 8.77, adj. p 2.1e-14; CLEC10A logFC 6.93, adj. p 1.5e-9; HLA-DQA1 logFC 4.83, adj. p 1.3e-15 | Not computed | 36 cells in cluster 5 | Wilcoxon (record setting) | find_markers |\n| Cluster 6, 13 cells: putative megakaryocytes | PPBP logFC 13.04, adj. p 7.7e-7; PF4 logFC 12.91, adj. p 7.7e-7; GNG11 logFC 12.43, adj. p 7.7e-7 | Not computed | 13 cells in cluster 6 | Wilcoxon (record setting) | find_markers |\n\nCheckpoint with clusters: cluster_leiden-5/leiden.h5ad. Cluster sizes: leiden_clusters.csv. Marker table: find_markers-1/markers.csv.\n\nUncertain:\n- Cluster count changes with resolution. The 5, 6 and 8 counts are from comparison runs. Marker genes are shown for resolution 0.7 only.\n- Clusters 5 and 6 are small (36 and 13 cells), so their labels are putative. Cluster 0 has no IL7R or CCR7 evidence, so no CD4 or CD8 split was made.\n- One donor and one sample. No test between conditions was run. Marker p-values are descriptive.\n\nWaits for you: Nothing.\n\nStep results that the answer does not mention, from the record:\n- n6 normalize_log: Scaled each cell to 10000 total counts and applied log1p. Raw counts are in layers['counts']. Log values are in .raw.\n- n8 scale_data: Scaled 1838 genes to unit variance, clipped at 10, after regressing out total_counts, pct_counts_mt.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Minimum genes per cell: 200 · Maximum genes per cell: 2500 · Maximum percent mitochondrial counts: 5 · Minimum cells per gene: 3 · Counts per cell after normalization: 10000 · Number of top highly variable genes (0 = use the mean and dispersion cutoffs): 0 · Variables to regress out: total_counts,pct_counts_mt · Number of principal components for the neighbor graph: 40 · Number of neighbors: 10 · Leiden resolution: 0.7 · Random seed: 0 · Marker gene test: wilcoxon.",
